{
  "name": "Start",
  "comment": "The builder appends the write-back set RIGHT AFTER the query, not at the step's end. In a step whose\nactions are [list.query, output.write], the set must land between them so it stores the query's result\nin %people% — if it landed after output.write, %people% would get output.write's result instead.\nWritten in formal to fix the action order (the writer picks it freely); it is the post-pass under test.",
  "step": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "set %people% = [{name: \"a\", age: 40}, {name: \"b\", age: 18}, {name: \"c\", age: 25}]",
      "line": {
        "number": 6
      },
